  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Advisory issued October 17 at 1:36PM EDT until October 17 at 2:30PM EDT by NWS Miami FL</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.

* WHERE...Southern Broward County in southeastern Florida...
Northern Miami-Dade County in southeastern Florida...

* WHEN...Until 230 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 136 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 2 and 3 inches of rain have
fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible over the
area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Hollywood, Hallandale, North Miami Beach, Aventura, West Park,
Ojus, Pembroke Park, Ives Estates and Hollywood Downtown.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
