   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in
Oklahoma...

North Fork Red River near Headrick affecting Jackson, Kiowa and
Tillman Counties.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.

* WHERE...North Fork Red River near Headrick.

* WHEN...Until this afternoon.

* IMPACTS...At 14.0 feet, Shallow flooding or isolation of
agricultural lands and rural roads occurs in Kiowa... Jackson...
and Tillman counties. Upstream points in Kiowa County may see
flooding several hours before the crest reaches the Headrick area.
The flood crest reaches downstream points near Tipton much later.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 8:00 AM CDT Saturday the stage was 14.4 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 13.5 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late
this morning and continue falling.
- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
