   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Advisory is extended for the following rivers in
Oklahoma...

Washita River at Anadarko affecting Caddo County.

* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.

* WHERE...Washita River at Anadarko.

* WHEN...Until late Sunday night.

* IMPACTS...At 18.0 feet, Expect near bankfull conditions along the
Washita River in eastern Caddo and western Grady counties.
Low-lying fields may become isolated by overflows from tributary
streams.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 7:30 AM CDT Saturday the stage was 17.9 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 19.0 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 18.5 feet
this evening.
- Action stage is 17.0 feet.
- Flood stage is 19.0 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
